<title>SWEDEN: Riksbank sees little risk of EU becoming federation.</title>
<headline>Riksbank sees little risk of EU becoming federation.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The governor of Sweden's central bank, Urban Backstrom, said on Friday there was little risk of the European Union (EU) developing into a federal union. &quot;A small country can block such a thing developing,&quot; Backstrom told a briefing on Europe's Economic and Monetary Union (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;A decision on the EU developing into a supranational organ can only be taken by a full majority. There is widespread scepticism about the EU developing into a federation.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
